course: dictionary
lesson: 7595
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on where you find them. Primary is one of these words. It can mean first in importance, first in time, or the first school you go to. The context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Luckily his primary head also wrote that Jake had improved a lot.» A primary head is the head teacher of a primary school. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A school fits, but a colour or a vote does not.
explain: «Friendships at primary school change a lot as children grow, and that is normal, not a failure.» Here primary school means the school for children aged about five to eleven. Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Primary means first in importance, first in order or time, or the main thing.
fact: A primary school is the first school children go to, for about ages five to eleven. In the USA it is called an elementary school.
fact: The primary colours are red, yellow and blue in paint, and red, green and blue in light on screens.
fact: A primary source is a first-hand record from the time, like a letter or a diary.
fact: In the USA, a primary is a vote to choose a party's candidate.
exercise: «Friendships at primary school change a lot as children grow.» What does primary school mean here? | A school that only teaches art | The most important school in the country | *The first school children go to, for about ages five to eleven | A school for grown-up students only
exercise: The primary colours are the colours that can be mixed to make many others. Which three are the primary colours in paint? | *Red, yellow and blue | Orange, purple and pink | Red, green and blue | Black, white and grey
exercise: Historians like a diary written at the time because it is a primary source. What is a primary source? | A story written a hundred years later | A map of the country | *A first-hand record from the time, like a letter or diary | A famous speech by a king
test: «The Primary Chronicle was put together around 1113, so historians check it against archaeology and foreign sources.» Why do historians check it? | Because it is too short to read | Because it was written yesterday | Because it has lots of pictures | *Because it mixes facts and legends
test: Sleep is of primary importance for a growing body. What does primary mean here? | Least important | A kind of paint | Last in order | *Most important, the main thing
exam: News reports said that in New Hampshire a robocall told people not to vote in a primary. What does primary mean here? | A first-hand record from history | *A vote to choose a party's candidate | A first school for young children | A colour that can be mixed to make others
